WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.440
Triangle A B C has an angle of forty-eight degrees at A

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.430
and sixty-seven degrees at B.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.710
The side B C is extended beyond C to a point D.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.090
Find the angle A C D, the angle outside the triangle.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.020
First find the angle inside the triangle at C.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.260
The three angles total one hundred and eighty.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.690
One hundred and eighty minus forty-eight minus

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.200
sixty-seven is sixty-five degrees.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.850
B, C and D lie on a straight line.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.270
The inside angle and the outside angle at C together

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:37.910
make one hundred and eighty.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.700
So the outside angle is one hundred and eighty minus

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.290
sixty-five: one hundred and fifteen degrees.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.575
Notice that forty-eight plus sixty-seven is also one

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:48.990
hundred and fifteen.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.230
That is no accident.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.840
The outside angle of a triangle always equals the sum of

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.050
the two inside angles furthest from it.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.250
Check with a different triangle.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.230
If the far angles were sixty and fifty-five,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.590
the inside angle at C would be sixty-five again,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.410
and the outside angle one hundred and fifteen.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.870
The shortcut and the long method agree.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.790
The outside angle equals the sum of the two

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.280
far inside angles.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.990
Rebuild this argument, then find the outside angle when

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.780
the far angles are thirty-five and eighty degrees.
